{"title": "Sectional Mock #57 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>K and L together can finish a work in 18 days. If K alone can finish the same work in 63 days, then in how many hours L alone finish the work?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; K &#2324;&#2352; L &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 18 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; K &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 63 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; L &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["21 days", "25.2 days", "17.8 days", "28 days"], "options_hi": ["21 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "25.2 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "17.8 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "28 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total work = LCM of 63 and 18 = 126 units</p><p>Efficiency of K and L together = 126/18 = 7 units/day</p><p>Efficiency of K = 126/63 = 2 units/day</p><p>Time taken L to complete the work = 126/(7-2) = 25.2 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total work = LCM of 63 and 18 = 126 units</p><p>Efficiency of K and L together = 126/18 = 7 units/day</p><p>Efficiency of K = 126/63 = 2 units/day</p><p>Time taken L to complete the work = 126/(7-2) = 25.2 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>If two polynomials x<sup>3</sup>  -  kx<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 28 and x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup>  -  2x + k leave the same remainder when divided by (x + 2), find the value of k and the remainder.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2346;&#2342; x<sup>3</sup> - kx<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 28 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup> - 2x + k &#2325;&#2379; (x + 2) &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; k &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["6/5", "3/5", "4/5", "7/5"], "options_hi": ["6/5", "3/5", "4/5", "7/5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>x + 2 = 0 =&gt; x = -2 </p><p>P(x) = x<sup>3</sup>  -  kx<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 28</p><p>P (-2) = -2<sup>3</sup>  -  k (-2)<sup>2</sup> + 4 * -2 + 28 = 12  -  4k </p><p>f (x) = x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup>  -  2x + k </p><p>f (-2) = -2<sup>3</sup> + (-2)<sup>2</sup>  -  6 * - 2 + k = k + 8 </p><p>p (x) = f (x) </p><p>12  -  4k = k + 8 </p><p>5k = 4</p><p>k = 4/5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x + 2 = 0 =&gt; x = -2 </p><p>P(x) = x<sup>3</sup>  -  kx<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 28</p><p>P (-2) = -2<sup>3</sup>  -  k (-2)<sup>2</sup> + 4 * -2 + 28 = 12  -  4k </p><p>f (x) = x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup>  -  2x + k </p><p>f (-2) = -2<sup>3</sup> + (-2)<sup>2</sup>  -  6 * - 2 + k = k + 8 </p><p>p (x) = f (x) </p><p>12  -  4k = k + 8 </p><p>5k = 4</p><p>k = 4/5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The perimeter of a circular lawn is 1232 m. There is 7 m wide path around the lawn. The area (in m<sup>2</sup>) of the path is: (take &pi; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2328;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 1232 m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; 7 m &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2341; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (m<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;: (&#960; = 22/7 &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;)</p>", "options_en": ["8778", "8558", "8800", "8756"], "options_hi": ["8778", "8558", "8800", "8756"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let radius of circular lawn = 'R' m</p><p>Perimeter of circular lawn = 2&#960;R = 1232</p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image062.png\"></p><p>R = 196 m</p><p>Area of path = Area of lawn with path  -  Area of lawn without path</p><p><img width=141 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image063.png\"></p><p><img width=127 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image064.png\"></p><p><img width=209 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image065.png\"></p><p><img width=95 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image067.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let radius of circular lawn = 'R' m</p><p>Perimeter of circular lawn = 2&#960;R = 1232</p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image062.png\"></p><p>R = 196 m</p><p>Area of path = Area of lawn with path  -  Area of lawn without path</p><p><img width=141 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image063.png\"></p><p><img width=127 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image064.png\"></p><p><img width=209 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image065.png\"></p><p><img width=95 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image067.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The value of [tan<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup>58&deg;]sec<sup>2</sup>58&deg;cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg; is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>[tan<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup>58&deg;]sec<sup>2</sup>58&deg;cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "-1", "-2"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "-1", "-2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>[tan<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup>58&deg;]sec<sup>2</sup>58&deg;cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= [sin<sup>2</sup>32&deg;/cos<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup>(90 - 32&deg;)]sec<sup>2</sup>(90 - 32&deg;)cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= sin<sup>2</sup>32&deg;(sec<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - 1)cosec<sup>2</sup>32&deg; cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= tan<sup>2</sup>32&deg;cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[tan<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup>58&deg;]sec<sup>2</sup>58&deg;cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= [sin<sup>2</sup>32&deg;/cos<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup>(90 - 32&deg;)]sec<sup>2</sup>(90 - 32&deg;)cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= sin<sup>2</sup>32&deg;(sec<sup>2</sup>32&deg; - 1)cosec<sup>2</sup>32&deg; cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= tan<sup>2</sup>32&deg;cot<sup>2</sup>32&deg;</p><p>= 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p><b>Directions:</b>Study the following information carefully and answer the related questions.</p><p>Following line-graph represents the data regarding monthly savings and monthly expenditure of six persons.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er221125st1m39-001.png\"></p><p>Monthly income = monthly expenditure + monthly savings</p><p>What is the respective ratio of monthly income of P to the monthly savings of Q and T together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p><b>&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358; :</b>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2331;&#2361; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er221125st1m39-001.png\"></p><p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351; = &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; + &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;</p><p>P &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; Q &#2324;&#2352; T &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["22: 21", "20: 19", "11: 10", "7: 6"], "options_hi": ["22: 21", "20: 19", "11: 10", "7: 6"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Here, monthly income of P = 44000</p><p>And, monthly savings of Q and T together = 28000 + 14000 = 42000</p><p>Therefore, ratio = 44000: 42000 = <b>22: 21</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, monthly income of P = 44000</p><p>And, monthly savings of Q and T together = 28000 + 14000 = 42000</p><p>Therefore, ratio = 44000: 42000 = <b>22: 21</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a circular race of 3000 m, A and B start from the same point and at the same time, at speeds of 24 km/h and 39 km/h, respectively. After what time will they meet for the first time on the track if they are running in the same direction?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>3000 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 24 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 39 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["780 sec", "640 sec", "720 sec", "540 sec"], "options_hi": ["780 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "640 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "720 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "540 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Relative speed = 39  -  24 = 15 km/h = 15 x 5/18 = 75/18 m/sec</p><p>Distance = 3000 m</p><p>Time taken by them to meet for the first time = 3000/ (75/18) = 720 sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative speed = 39  -  24 = 15 km/h = 15 x 5/18 = 75/18 m/sec</p><p>Distance = 3000 m</p><p>Time taken by them to meet for the first time = 3000/ (75/18) = 720 sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A retailer sells clothes at some profit on the cost price but uses a false measuring tape of 80 cm instead of 1 metre. If his overall profit percentage is 45%, then find the profit percentage on the cost price.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; 1 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; 80 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2347;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 45% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["12%", "18%", "25%", "16%"], "options_hi": ["12%", "18%", "25%", "16%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let cost price of 1 meter of cloth = &#8377;100</p><p>Cost price of 80 cm cloth = &#8377;80</p><p>Overall profit percentage = 45%</p><p>Selling price of cloth = 145% of 80 = &#8377;116</p><p>Profit percentage = [(116  -  100)/100] *100 = 16%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let cost price of 1 meter of cloth = &#8377;100</p><p>Cost price of 80 cm cloth = &#8377;80</p><p>Overall profit percentage = 45%</p><p>Selling price of cloth = 145% of 80 = &#8377;116</p><p>Profit percentage = [(116  -  100)/100] *100 = 16%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of ages of A and B, 4 years ago was 7 : 10 and the ratio of their ages after 6 years will be 4 : 5. What is the present age of B?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;, A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 7 : 10 &#2341;&#2366; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4 : 5 &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["20 years", "22 years", "24 years", "26 years"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "22 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "24 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "26 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the age of A and B 4 years ago is 7x and 10x respectively</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(7x + 10)/(10x + 10) = 4/5</p><p>35x + 50 = 40x + 40</p><p>5x = 10</p><p>x = 2</p><p>Age of B = 10 * 2 + 4 = 24 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the age of A and B 4 years ago is 7x and 10x respectively</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(7x + 10)/(10x + 10) = 4/5</p><p>35x + 50 = 40x + 40</p><p>5x = 10</p><p>x = 2</p><p>Age of B = 10 * 2 + 4 = 24 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>18 women can complete a piece of job in 40 days, then how many additional women will be required to complete 120% of the work in 12 days?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>18 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; 40 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; 12 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 120% &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["54", "56", "58", "52"], "options_hi": ["54", "56", "58", "52"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let x number of additional women will be required</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>M<sub>1</sub>D<sub>1</sub>/W<sub>1</sub> = M<sub>2</sub>D<sub>2</sub>/W<sub>2</sub></p><p>=&gt; (18 * 40)/100 = ((18 + x) * 12)/120</p><p>=&gt; 36/5 = (x + 18)/10</p><p>=&gt; x = 54</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let x number of additional women will be required</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>M<sub>1</sub>D<sub>1</sub>/W<sub>1</sub> = M<sub>2</sub>D<sub>2</sub>/W<sub>2</sub></p><p>=&gt; (18 * 40)/100 = ((18 + x) * 12)/120</p><p>=&gt; 36/5 = (x + 18)/10</p><p>=&gt; x = 54</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is a perfect cube?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2328;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1000000", "2160000", "194000", "12500000"], "options_hi": ["1000000", "2160000", "194000", "12500000"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Y*Z = 75 = 1 * 3 * 5 * 5</p><p>Pairs of YZ = (1, 75), (3, 25), (5, 15)</p><p>Y  -  Z = 75  -  1 = 74</p><p>Or 25  -  3 = 22</p><p>Or 15  -  5 = 10 </p><p>Hence, option 'b' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Y*Z = 75 = 1 * 3 * 5 * 5</p><p>Pairs of YZ = (1, 75), (3, 25), (5, 15)</p><p>Y  -  Z = 75  -  1 = 74</p><p>Or 25  -  3 = 22</p><p>Or 15  -  5 = 10 </p><p>Hence, option 'b' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three glass mugs are selected from six distinct glass mugs and a ceramic mug are selected from eight distinct ceramic mugs. In how many ways can the four mugs be arranged on a rack in a coffee shop if a glass mug must be placed at the beginning of the rack?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2331;&#2361; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2327;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2327; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2336; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2327; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2364;&#2368; &#2358;&#2377;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2327; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["2880", "1440", "1920", "1600"], "options_hi": ["2880", "1440", "1920", "1600"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total glass and ceramic mugs are 6 and 8 respectively.</p><p>Total number of ways to select 3 glass mugs and a ceramic mug when a glass mug placed at the beginning of the rack = 3 * <sup>5</sup>C<sub>2</sub> * <sup>8</sup>C<sub>1</sub> * 3!</p><p>= 3 * [(5*4)/(2*1)] * 8 * 3!</p><p>= 3*10*8*6</p><p>= 1440</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total glass and ceramic mugs are 6 and 8 respectively.</p><p>Total number of ways to select 3 glass mugs and a ceramic mug when a glass mug placed at the beginning of the rack = 3 * <sup>5</sup>C<sub>2</sub> * <sup>8</sup>C<sub>1</sub> * 3!</p><p>= 3 * [(5*4)/(2*1)] * 8 * 3!</p><p>= 3*10*8*6</p><p>= 1440</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cylindrical tank of radius 14 cm is full of water. If 616 litres of water are drawn out, then the water level in the tank is dropped by ______ m. (Take &#960; = (22/7) )</p>", "q_hi": "14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 616 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; ______ &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; (&#960; = (22/7) &#2354;&#2375;&#2306;)", "options_en": ["1000", "100", "1", "10"], "options_hi": ["1000", "100", "1", "10"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>We know that volume of a cylindrical tank = &#960; *r<sup>2</sup>*h</p><p>Radius = 14cm</p><p>So volume = (22/7)*14*14*h</p><p>Now if 616 litres are drawn out, so reduction in height =</p><p>(22/7)*14*14*h =616*1000 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>h= 1000 cm</p><p>so h = 10m</p><p>option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that volume of a cylindrical tank = &#960; *r<sup>2</sup>*h</p><p>Radius = 14cm</p><p>So volume = (22/7)*14*14*h</p><p>Now if 616 litres are drawn out, so reduction in height =</p><p>(22/7)*14*14*h =616*1000 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>h= 1000 cm</p><p>so h = 10m</p><p>option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person borrowed 8100 at 8 % annual simple interest repayable in 3 equal annual installments. What will be the annual installment?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; 8% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 8100 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; 3 &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 3000", "Rs. 3100", "Rs. 2900", "Rs. 2800"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 3000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 3100", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2900", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2800"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>S.I = P * R * T/100</p><p></p><p>= 8100 * 8 * 3/100</p><p></p><p>= Rs. 1944</p><p></p><p>A = Amount = 8100 + 1944 = Rs. 10044</p><p></p><p>T = Time</p><p></p><p>R = rate</p><p></p><p>Installment = (A * 100)/ [T * 100 + (Tn - 1 + Tn - 2 +  + 1) * R]</p><p></p><p>= (10044 * 100)/ [3 * 100 + (2 + 1) * 8]</p><p></p><p>= (10044 * 100)/ 324</p><p></p><p>= Rs. 3100</p><p></p><p>Hence, annual instalment = Rs. 3100</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S.I = P * R * T/100</p><p></p><p>= 8100 * 8 * 3/100</p><p></p><p>= Rs. 1944</p><p></p><p>A = Amount = 8100 + 1944 = Rs. 10044</p><p></p><p>T = Time</p><p></p><p>R = rate</p><p></p><p>Installment = (A * 100)/ [T * 100 + (Tn - 1 + Tn - 2 +  + 1) * R]</p><p></p><p>= (10044 * 100)/ [3 * 100 + (2 + 1) * 8]</p><p></p><p>= (10044 * 100)/ 324</p><p></p><p>= Rs. 3100</p><p></p><p>Hence, annual instalment = Rs. 3100</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe M can fill a cistern in  (81/2) minutes. There is a leakage at the bottom of the cistern, due to which it takes (189/4) minutes for the cistern to be filled. How much time will the leakage take in emptying the cistern, if the cistern is completely filled initially?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; M &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; (81/2) &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; (189/4) &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2349;&#2352; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2379;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2352;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["561/2 minutes", "563/2 minutes", "567/2 minutes", "565/2 minutes"], "options_hi": ["561/2 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "563/2 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "567/2 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "565/2 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Pipe M can fill a cistern in = 81/2 minutes</p><p>And pipe M with leakage can fill the cistern in = 189/4 minutes</p><p>So, leakage alone can empty the tank in = 1/(2/81  -  4/189) = 567/2 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Pipe M can fill a cistern in = 81/2 minutes</p><p>And pipe M with leakage can fill the cistern in = 189/4 minutes</p><p>So, leakage alone can empty the tank in = 1/(2/81  -  4/189) = 567/2 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (4x  -  7y)<sup>2 </sup>+ (5y  -  3z)<sup>2</sup> = 0, then find x : y : z = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (4x - 7y)<sup>2 </sup>+ (5y - 3z)<sup>2</sup> = 0, &#2340;&#2379; x : y : z = ? &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["21 : 20 : 15", "21 : 12 : 20", "22 : 21 : 20", "21 : 20 : 12"], "options_hi": ["21 : 20 : 15", "21 : 12 : 20", "22 : 21 : 20", "21 : 20 : 12"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>If a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>=&gt; a = 0 and b = 0</p><p>(4x  -  7y)<sup>2</sup> + (5y  -  3z)<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>4x  -  7y = 0</p><p>4x = 7y</p><p>x : y = 7 : 4........(i)</p><p>5y  -  3z = 0</p><p>5y = 3z</p><p>y : z = 3 : 5.......(ii)</p><p>multiply eq(i) by 3 and eq(ii) by 4 we get,</p><p>x : y : z = 21 : 12 : 20</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>=&gt; a = 0 and b = 0</p><p>(4x  -  7y)<sup>2</sup> + (5y  -  3z)<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>4x  -  7y = 0</p><p>4x = 7y</p><p>x : y = 7 : 4........(i)</p><p>5y  -  3z = 0</p><p>5y = 3z</p><p>y : z = 3 : 5.......(ii)</p><p>multiply eq(i) by 3 and eq(ii) by 4 we get,</p><p>x : y : z = 21 : 12 : 20</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>From a container containing milk and water solution, a boy took out 20 litres of solution and poured the equal quantity of water, then the ratio of milk to water became 12: 13. If he again takes out 12.5 litres of solution and mixes the equal quantity of water, the ratio of milk to water would become 21: 29. What was the quantity of solution contained in the container?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375; 20 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 12:13 &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 12.5 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 21:29 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["120 litres", "100 litres", "125 litres", "150 litres"], "options_hi": ["120 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "100 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "125 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "150 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>In this question, we will go from the last information</p><p>In a solution, the ratio of milk to water = 12: 13</p><p>Let the quantity of milk be 12a litres and the quantity of water be 13a litres</p><p>In 12.5 litres solution,</p><p>The quantity of milk = 12*12.5/25 = 6 litres</p><p>Quantity of water = 12.5  -  6 = 6.5 litres</p><p>Thus, (12a  -  6)/(13a  -  6.5 + 12.5) = 21/29</p><p>(12a  -  6)/(13a + 6) = 21/29</p><p>By solving, a = 4 litres</p><p>It means, total quantity of solution = 12a + 13a = 25a = 100 litres</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In this question, we will go from the last information</p><p>In a solution, the ratio of milk to water = 12: 13</p><p>Let the quantity of milk be 12a litres and the quantity of water be 13a litres</p><p>In 12.5 litres solution,</p><p>The quantity of milk = 12*12.5/25 = 6 litres</p><p>Quantity of water = 12.5  -  6 = 6.5 litres</p><p>Thus, (12a  -  6)/(13a  -  6.5 + 12.5) = 21/29</p><p>(12a  -  6)/(13a + 6) = 21/29</p><p>By solving, a = 4 litres</p><p>It means, total quantity of solution = 12a + 13a = 25a = 100 litres</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>The HCF and LCM of two numbers is 18 and 108 respectively. If one number is 50% more than the other number, then find the larger number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2324;&#2352; LCM &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 18 &#2324;&#2352; 108 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 50% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["54", "72", "90", "36"], "options_hi": ["54", "72", "90", "36"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let one number = 2a</p><p>Other number = 150% of 2a = 3a </p><p>Now,</p><p>2a*3a = 18*108</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> = 18*18</p><p>a = 18</p><p>So, larger number = 3*18 = 54</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let one number = 2a</p><p>Other number = 150% of 2a = 3a </p><p>Now,</p><p>2a*3a = 18*108</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> = 18*18</p><p>a = 18</p><p>So, larger number = 3*18 = 54</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If x = (&radic;6 + 2) and y =(&radic;6 &#8722; 2), then what is the value of (&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">x", "q_hi": "<p><div><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x = (&radic;6 + 2) &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; y =(&radic;6 &#8722; 2) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379;(&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">x", "options_en": ["42", "97", "35", "22"], "options_hi": ["42", "97", "35", "22"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Compute x/y:</p><p>Multiply numerator and denominator by (&radic;6 + 2):</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x/y = ( (&radic;6 + 2)&#178; ) / ( (&radic;6)&#178; &#8722; 2&#178; )</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;= (6 + 4&radic;6 + 4) / (6 &#8722; 4)</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;= (10 + 4&radic;6) / 2 = 5 + 2&radic;6.</p><p>Similarly, compute y/x:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;y/x = 5 &#8722; 2&radic;6.</p><p>Sum the two:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x/y + y/x = (5 + 2&radic;6) + (5 &#8722; 2&radic;6) = 10.</p><p>Then, (x/y + y/x)&#178; &#8722; 3 = 10&#178; &#8722; 3 = 100 &#8722; 3 = 97.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Compute x/y:</p><p>Multiply numerator and denominator by (&radic;6 + 2):</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x/y = ( (&radic;6 + 2)&#178; ) / ( (&radic;6)&#178; &#8722; 2&#178; )</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;= (6 + 4&radic;6 + 4) / (6 &#8722; 4)</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;&#8195;= (10 + 4&radic;6) / 2 = 5 + 2&radic;6.</p><p>Similarly, compute y/x:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;y/x = 5 &#8722; 2&radic;6.</p><p>Sum the two:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x/y + y/x = (5 + 2&radic;6) + (5 &#8722; 2&radic;6) = 10.</p><p>Then, (x/y + y/x)&#178; &#8722; 3 = 10&#178; &#8722; 3 = 100 &#8722; 3 = 97.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Let the HCF of X and Y be 'M' and let Y = MN. LCM of X and Y is given by:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 'M' &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; Y = MN &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["XN", "MN", "YN", "XY"], "options_hi": ["XN", "MN", "YN", "XY"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>We know that,</p><p>HCF * LCM = product of numbers</p><p>M * LCM = X * Y</p><p>LCM = X * MN/M</p><p>LCM = XN</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that,</p><p>HCF * LCM = product of numbers</p><p>M * LCM = X * Y</p><p>LCM = X * MN/M</p><p>LCM = XN</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two chairs and one fan cost Rs.14000, while two fans and one chair cost Rs.19600. The value of one fan is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 14000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 19600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.7200", "Rs.8400", "Rs.10600", "Rs.6400"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.7200", "&#2352;&#2369;.8400", "&#2352;&#2369;.10600", "&#2352;&#2369;.6400"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost of one fan and one chair be Rs. X and Rs. Y respectively.</p><p>Given that,</p><p>2Y + X = 14000 ... (1)</p><p>And</p><p>2X + Y = 19600 ... (2)</p><p>Solving equations (1) and (2),</p><p>X = 8400</p><p>Value of one fan = Rs.8400</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost of one fan and one chair be Rs. X and Rs. Y respectively.</p><p>Given that,</p><p>2Y + X = 14000 ... (1)</p><p>And</p><p>2X + Y = 19600 ... (2)</p><p>Solving equations (1) and (2),</p><p>X = 8400</p><p>Value of one fan = Rs.8400</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>The radius of a sphere is &radic;5 times the radius of another sphere. What is the ratio of surface area of bigger sphere to that of smaller sphere?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &radic;5 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["25: 1", "1: 25", "5: 1", "1: 5"], "options_hi": ["25: 1", "1: 25", "5: 1", "1: 5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Radius of smaller sphere * &radic;5 = Radius of bigger sphere</p><p>Required ratio = 4&#960; * (radius of bigger sphere)<sup>2</sup>/ 4&#960; * (radius of smaller sphere)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= (&radic;5/1)<sup>2</sup> = 5: 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius of smaller sphere * &radic;5 = Radius of bigger sphere</p><p>Required ratio = 4&#960; * (radius of bigger sphere)<sup>2</sup>/ 4&#960; * (radius of smaller sphere)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= (&radic;5/1)<sup>2</sup> = 5: 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A dishonest dealer marks up his goods by 50% and then gives a discount of 20% on the marked price. Apart from this, he uses a faulty balance which reads 1kg for 900 gm. What is his net profit percentage (rounded off to the nearest integer)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2312;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2346;&#2352; 50% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2379;&#2359;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366; (&#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2370;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; 900 gm &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 1kg &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335;&#2340;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;)</p>", "options_en": ["24", "27", "36", "33"], "options_hi": ["24", "27", "36", "33"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let cost price of the goods = &#8377;1000 per kg</p><p>Marked price = 150% of 1000 = &#8377;1500</p><p>Selling price = (100-20)% of 1500 = &#8377;1200</p><p>Since, he uses 900gm weight instead of 1kg-</p><p>CP of the goods = &#8377;900</p><p>Profit = 1200  -  900 = &#8377;300</p><p>Profit% =(300/900) *100 = 33%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let cost price of the goods = &#8377;1000 per kg</p><p>Marked price = 150% of 1000 = &#8377;1500</p><p>Selling price = (100-20)% of 1500 = &#8377;1200</p><p>Since, he uses 900gm weight instead of 1kg-</p><p>CP of the goods = &#8377;900</p><p>Profit = 1200  -  900 = &#8377;300</p><p>Profit% =(300/900) *100 = 33%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a group of N number of boys, a new boy weighing 62 kg joins, then the average weight of the group increased by 1 kg. If the weight of the new boy had been 50 kg, then the average weight of the boys would have decreased by 1 kg. The actual average weight of the group is?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>N &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 62 kg &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2351;&#2366; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 1 kg &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2344;&#2319; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 50 kg &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 1 kg &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["56 kg", "54 kg", "55 kg", "51 kg"], "options_hi": ["56 kg", "54 kg", "55 kg", "51 kg"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Average weight is increased by 1 when the weight of new boy is 62 kg and the same is decreased by 1 when the weight of new boy is 50 kg. So, the weight on which the average weight of group does not affect, will be the average of 62 and 50, and that is 56 kg.</p><p>So, the actual average weight of the group is 56 kg.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Average weight is increased by 1 when the weight of new boy is 62 kg and the same is decreased by 1 when the weight of new boy is 50 kg. So, the weight on which the average weight of group does not affect, will be the average of 62 and 50, and that is 56 kg.</p><p>So, the actual average weight of the group is 56 kg.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A can fill a tank at 25 m<sup>3</sup>/minute. Pipe A and pipe B together can fill the same tank in 12 minutes. If the volume of the tank is 500 m<sup>3</sup>, then find the time taken by pipe B to fill the tank alone.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 25 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>/&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; 500 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["25 minutes", "36 minutes", "40 minutes", "30 minutes"], "options_hi": ["25 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "36 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "40 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of the tank = 500 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>Time taken by pipe A = 500/25 = 20 minutes</p><p>Total capacity (LCM of 20 and 12) = 60 units</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A = 60/20 = 3 units/minute</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A and B together = 60/12 = 5 units/minute</p><p>Time taken by pipe B to fill the tank = 60/(5 - 3) = 30 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of the tank = 500 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>Time taken by pipe A = 500/25 = 20 minutes</p><p>Total capacity (LCM of 20 and 12) = 60 units</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A = 60/20 = 3 units/minute</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A and B together = 60/12 = 5 units/minute</p><p>Time taken by pipe B to fill the tank = 60/(5 - 3) = 30 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>C and A together can complete a piece of work in 15 days. B alone can complete it in 30 days. If the work done by C in one day is equal to the work done by A and B together in 1 day. In how many days C alone can complete the same piece of work?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; C &#2324;&#2352; A &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 15 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; B &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 30 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2327;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; C &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["20 days", "24 days", "23 days", "28 days"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "24 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "23 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "28 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>According to question,</p><p>C's efficiency = (A + B)'s efficiency.......... (i)</p><p>Total work = LCM of 15 and 30 = 30 unit</p><p>Efficiency of B = 30/30 = 1 unit</p><p>Efficiency of (A + C) = 30/15 = 2 unit</p><p>Efficiency of (A + B + C) = 3 unit........ (ii)</p><p>Or 2 C's efficiency = 3 unit</p><p>C's efficiency = 1.5 unit</p><p>Time taken by C alone to complete the whole work = 30/1.5 = 20 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to question,</p><p>C's efficiency = (A + B)'s efficiency.......... (i)</p><p>Total work = LCM of 15 and 30 = 30 unit</p><p>Efficiency of B = 30/30 = 1 unit</p><p>Efficiency of (A + C) = 30/15 = 2 unit</p><p>Efficiency of (A + B + C) = 3 unit........ (ii)</p><p>Or 2 C's efficiency = 3 unit</p><p>C's efficiency = 1.5 unit</p><p>Time taken by C alone to complete the whole work = 30/1.5 = 20 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}]}